Here are some rules:
- Use type for everything except for a class that should implement some interface.
- If a type is used only one place, place it directly in that component file.
- If a type is used two or more places, place it in server/shared/types.ts/shared/interfaces.ts
- If a utility is used only once place, place it directly in that component file.
- If the same utility is used two or more places, place it in the server/shared/utils.ts file.
- For each of the types/interfaces/utils found in the shared module, include a detailed comment in their definitions that specifies what they do and how they are supposed to be used. In addition, types/interfaces that are related should be located around the same lines and separated with others using // --------------------------- comment.  For specifying the groups they belong to, include //----------------- DESCRIPTION OF GROUP ------------ comment before the types/interfaces/utils are used.
- No utils/types/interfaces files found in a specific module. This is because keeping track of different types/utils to decrease code-deduplication is a very arduous task. It's better to have just one shared file for each.
- Routes for the backend should just call a service after parsing the given input in appropriate format for the service. A route may use one or more services. A service may also use one more different services. 
- If there is anything that can potentially be confusing, include a comment for it.

